      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'd like to bump this as well! I ended up writing a program that intercepts my eye tracking program, by configuring it send to a port my program is listening to instead of directly to VR Chat. It then reads the /tracking/eye/EyesClosedAmount address, then sends out an /avatar/parameters/EyesClosed float value for my avatar. I then just redirect all the packets to VRChat on port 9000.\n\nIt works, but all of that just to make it so my avatars ears can react and twitch with my blinking. Having these as default parameters to toy around with would be amazing. Think of the possibilities. Imagine a horror world being able to react to someone closing their eyes!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
